    {
      "id": "p0147-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby didn't note it at the time, but these phrases are references to the English version of Super Mario World, a classic Super Nintendo game released in 1991. Specifically, these are the names of eight secret stages that require great expertise to complete. Unfortunately, the original Japanese version of Super Mario World used much simpler - and milder - names for these same stages:",
        "raw": "Toby didn't note it at the time, but these phrases are references to the English\nversion of Super Mario World, a classic Super Nintendo game released in\n1991. Specifically, these are the names of eight secret stages that require great\nexpertise to complete. Unfortunately, the original Japanese version of Super\nMario World used much simpler - and milder - names for these same stages:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09370873,
          0.30740714,
          0.68548136,
          0.3922
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09168194,
          0.30669286,
          0.70043908,
          0.39327143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Toby 当时没有标注，但这些词引用了 1991 年发行的超级任天堂经典游戏 Super Mario World 的英语版。具体来说，它们是八个高难度隐藏关卡的名称。遗憾的是，Super Mario World 日语原版给这些关卡起的名字要简单、温和得多：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 56,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 105,
